        "id": 1130416
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-03T09:54:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EC_CMD_HOST_EVENT_SET_WAKE_MASK is used by coreboot to set wake mask on S3 entry/Exit. S0ix sleep state doesn\u0027t take SMI handler flow  like S3 (no coreboot flow in S0ix entry/exit) . So coreboot cannot set WAKE mask on S0ix entry and exit. \n\nWith the new host command, on boot coreboot can notify the wake mask to EC with the EC_CMD_SET_S0IX_WAKE_MASK command and EC stores this. On S0ix entry/exit, EC configure the LPC_HOST_EVENT_WAKE mask. This helps to define the wake mask in a single place (Coreboot)",
      "parentUuid": "a94d00e4_d1b653c2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3506,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 3506,
        "endChar": 19
      },
