      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"With the new host command, on boot coreboot can notify the wake mask to EC with the EC_CMD_SET_S0IX_WAKE_MASK command and EC stores this. On S0ix entry/exit, EC configure the LPC_HOST_EVENT_WAKE mask. This helps to define the wake mask in a single place (Coreboot)\"\n\nThis is the part that I find inconsistent. If we have settings that can become active on the edge of power transitions why don\u0027t we do that all the time? I guess it\u0027d be a lot of change from the current semantics, but it seems odd to have a mask lurking for use but the other host event masks are not that way.",
